  GEOG480:{name:"Cartography and Geovisualization", term:"Fall", units:3, prereq:"GEOG 231 or GEOG 380", antireq:"GEOG 480 and GEOG 437", description:"Focuses on mapping technologies for cartography and geo-visualization. The role of cartography and geovisualization is explored both theoretically, and practically in the communication of spatial data. In lecture and lab-based settings, examines data considerations, map design fundamentals and techniques, map use and interactive design for the communication of geographic information."},
